    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text_31587cb1e6835bdf",
      "x": 405,
      "y": 105,
      "width": 392,
      "height": 244,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "baseFontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "fontWeight": 400,
      "text": "1. Generates segmentation mask for object and generates LiDAR points frustum.\n2. Random points are sampled inside the mask and using the closes LiDAR point depth is given to the sampled point. Then projected to 3D.\n3. Main reason they do this is because LiDAR cant detect far away objects and this creates virtual points.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 18,
      "containerId": "rect_31587cb1e6835bdf",
      "originalText": "1. Generates segmentation mask for object and generates LiDAR points frustum.\n2. Random points are sampled inside the mask and using the closes LiDAR point depth is given to the sampled point. Then projected to 3D.\n3. Main reason they do this is because LiDAR cant detect far away objects and this creates virtual points.",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 4408,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1720000000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "id": "rect_1417ad984497c2b4",
      "x": 700,
      "y": 100,
      "width": 515,
      "height": 240,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 8550,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "text_1417ad984497c2b4",
